# Example environment configuration for ai-bank-pricing-engine.
#
# The engine has no dotenv loader: EnvSecretsProvider (secrets/provider.py)
# reads only the real process environment via os.environ, deliberately --
# secrets live in the environment, never in a config file. So copying this
# to `.env` does nothing by itself. To use it locally:
#
#   cp .env.example .env    # fill in the values you need
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#
# (never commit `.env` with real values -- it is already covered by
# .gitignore), or set these as real environment variables / secrets in your
# deployment. Every value below is optional: each feature it gates is off by
# default and the engine runs fine with none of this set.

# --- Pricing intelligence: database location -------------------------------
# Overrides PricingIntelligenceConfig.database_path (default:
# data/processed/pricing_intelligence/observations.db). Useful when the
# operational database should live outside the repo checkout.
PRICING_INTELLIGENCE_DB_PATH=

# --- Pricing intelligence: alert delivery -----------------------------------
# Generic webhook (Slack / Microsoft Teams / Discord-compatible). See
# docs/pricing_intelligence.md for the exact JSON shape posted.
PRICING_INTELLIGENCE_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Telegram bot delivery. Both must be set for Telegram alerts to send; either
# alone is treated as "not configured". Create a bot via @BotFather to get a
# token, and message the bot (or add it to a group) to get a chat id.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# --- LLM decision-support layer (src/balance_pricing_engine/llm/) ----------
# Required only for examples/run_llm_diagnostics.py and the model-validation
# narration agent. Every response from that layer is tagged
# [DECISION-SUPPORT: requires human review] and never wired into automated
# pricing decisions.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Optional FastAPI serving layer -----------------------------------------
# Comma-separated API keys accepted by the `X-API-Key` header on
# POST /run-scenario and POST /v1/pricing/scenarios. Unset disables auth
# entirely (fine for local development, not for a reachable deployment).
#
# Left commented out, unlike every other line above: api/auth.py's
# require_api_key() deliberately treats "set but empty" as a *misconfigured*
# secret and fails closed with a 500 on every protected request, distinct
# from "unset" (auth disabled). Following this file's own recommended
# workflow (`cp .env.example .env` then `source .env`) would otherwise export
# this as an empty string rather than leaving it unset, silently breaking the
# API the moment auth is not being configured. Uncomment and fill in a real
# value to enable auth.
# PRICING_ENGINE_API_KEYS=
